Hanumān combs Laṅkā houses ponds rivers woods and misses Sītā --- Hanumān fears Sītā fallen drowned eaten or caged by Rāvaṇa --- Hanumān dreads ill news killing Rāma Lakṣmaṇa Bharata mothers Sugrīva and monkeys --- Hanumān refuses return to Kiṣkindhā without Sītā and vows forest life --- Hanumān vows to kill Rāvaṇa or carry him to Rāma --- Hanumān resolves to live and comb Laṅkā and Aśōkavana again --- Hanumān prays gods for success and turns toward unsearched Aśōkavana
